  "goodToKnow": "Die Tragfähigkeit is load capacity, of bridges, floors and ships, and figuratively viability or soundness: die Tragfähigkeit eines Konzepts, einer Koalition. Many German motorway bridges from the 1960s and 70s have lost Tragfähigkeit; the Carolabrücke in Dresden partly collapsed in 2024. Tragfähig means load-bearing or workable. It has no plural."
